<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Testing on Kairos Lab</title><link>https://leekairos.github.io/en/tags/testing/</link><description>Recent content in Testing on Kairos Lab</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://leekairos.github.io/en/tags/testing/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Test Post: Kairos Lab Blog Is Live</title><link>https://leekairos.github.io/en/p/kairos-blog-test/</link><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://leekairos.github.io/en/p/kairos-blog-test/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://leekairos.github.io/p/kairos-blog-test/cover.jpg" alt="Featured image of post Test Post: Kairos Lab Blog Is Live" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the new Kairos Lab blog. This is the first test post, here to check that Hugo + Stack renders everything properly: headings, table of contents, code blocks, the cover image, word count, and estimated reading time.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you can see this post, the blog is live.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="why-hugo--stack"&gt;Why Hugo + Stack&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hugo is a static site generator written in Go, and its biggest strength is speed: even a thousand posts build in seconds. It needs no database and no server — push the Markdown and it becomes a website.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Stack is a card-style Hugo theme made for blogging, and it ships with:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Responsive layout that looks good on phones and computers&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A dark-mode toggle in the top right&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Local search, archives, categories, and tags&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Table of contents, reading time, and related-post recommendations&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="previewing-locally-and-publishing"&gt;Previewing locally and publishing&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When writing locally, start the preview server first — save a change and it shows up in the browser right away:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Start the local preview (-D shows drafts too)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;hugo server -D&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Open http://localhost:1313&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once it looks right, push to GitHub and Actions builds and publishes it automatically:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git add content/post/kairos-blog-test.md&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git commit -m &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Publish test post&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git push origin main&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="what-a-posts-front-matter-looks-like"&gt;What a post&amp;rsquo;s front matter looks like&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every post starts with front matter — the title, date, categories, and tags:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;7&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nn"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;I Saved 1,000 Articles — Why Can&amp;#39;t I Use a Single One?&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ld"&gt;2026-11-14&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;categories&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;From Collecting to a Second Brain&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Knowledge Management&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Collecting&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Inbox&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nn"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A post with &lt;code&gt;draft: true&lt;/code&gt; is a draft and won&amp;rsquo;t be published; set it to &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; and it appears on the site.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="whats-coming-next"&gt;What&amp;rsquo;s coming next&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first real post is already written: &amp;ldquo;I Saved 1,000 Articles — Why Can&amp;rsquo;t I Use a Single One?&amp;rdquo;, built on my own numbers: 621 notes, 337 sitting in the Inbox, and only 16 in the knowledge base.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Once this test post confirms the layout is fine, Episode 1 goes out. Stay tuned.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;</description></item></channel></rss>